It's not just item exploding, though; it's monster resistance.  Most
of the tough stuff in Gehennom resists Firebrand, for instance, and
most of Air/Astral resist Mjollnir.

Basically, they become regular weapons of their time (and war hammers
pretty much suck) at points in the game where you need to do the most
damage.

I don't bother min/maxing much, if I get any of Grayswandir,
Excalibur, Excalibur, Stormbringer, Sceptre of Might, Vorpy, Fire
Brand, Frost Brand, Sunsword, Werebane, Mjollnir then I'm fine with
it, but I'll normally prefer weapons toward the beginning of that list
if I have the option.  Magicbane is a special case depending on the
character, but it's probably close to Grayswandir in desirability.
And circumstances matter; e.g I'll usually go with Mjollnir early on
until I can enchant something else up (unless I luck into grayswandir
or something).

